// Q-022 `request` cannot be read in a helper, though session() can: a helper reading a cookie must be passed `request`
// mode: serve
// get: / cookie=tz=480
// open-when: only exists in routes
// open-when: unknown name `cookie`
// fixed-when: /GET \/ -> 200\n480/
// From FEEDBACK2.md §10 (found on 896e758). `request` in helpers stays a design choice; the fix
// asked for was `cookie(name)`, which reads one in any function the request runs (fe10f8c).

fn tz() = cookie("tz") ?? "0"

route GET / = tz()
